[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2859842511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2859842511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2859842511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qdbvP","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T18:39:47Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T19:27:13Z","body":"- See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100452\r\n\r\nPerhaps we can use the Roslyn Analyzer to prohibit dynamic strings and only allow the implicit conversion of constant strings to avoid cache increases, but breaks compatibility.\r\n\r\nHowever, I still think #100452 is a good approach which doesn't need Roslyn Analyzer at all, but it was vetoed\r\nhttps://chat.godotengine.org/channel/dotnet?msg=LxpDpib8R4Q6oW6c6.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2859842511/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2862643746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2862643746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2862643746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qoHoi","user":{"login":"lrahmann","id":9094802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9094802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann","html_url":"https://github.com/lrahmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T11:02:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T11:02:57Z","body":"Nice :) \r\nBut,...\r\nThis can cause memory leaks e.g when using dynamic strings and casting them to StringName (The ConcurrentDictionary<T,V> keeps the reference alive). Using [ConditionalWeakTable<String,StringName>](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.runtime.compilerservices.conditionalweaktable-2)  should be the better option (This adds a GC reference from String->StringName and nothing else. So when String is freed so is StringName). If the string is a global constant it will never be freed anyway so this functions basically the same. \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2862643746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2862765854","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2862765854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2862765854,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qolce","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T11:51:28Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T11:51:28Z","body":"#100452 uses WeakReference and remove itself from ConcurrentDictionary in Dispose() to clear unused StringName, which may be better than ConditionalWeakTable. ConditionalWeakTable can't remove cache if the string is referenced in other places.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2862765854/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2863023564","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2863023564","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2863023564,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qpkXM","user":{"login":"lrahmann","id":9094802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9094802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann","html_url":"https://github.com/lrahmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T13:13:00Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T14:41:44Z","body":"@beicause \r\n**edited**\r\n~~maybe I'm missing something here, but having it in Dispose will prevent it from being cleared by the finalizer because the finalizer can't be called until Dispose.~~\r\n\r\n**Okay I just saw that you are using weak references in the Dictionary over there. I only looked shortly but then you may free these referenced StringName instances as soon as these calls are over ? Additionally this places another reference on the strings themselves which may leak if string are created dynamically and not interned**\r\n\r\nYou are always free to explicitly remove it from  the ConditionalWeakTable during Dispose while the string stays referenced? \r\n\r\nBut as for casts for Godot native types, I would use a separate Dictionary<uint, StringName>(?) similar to the above, the two structures can overlap but you don't want to create a unnecessary string object when you only want the StringName one.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2863023564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2863254581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2863254581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2863254581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qqcw1","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T14:22:56Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T14:22:56Z","body":"There are no memory leaks, this is fully managed. I also don’t believe removing them is beneficial because 1. There’s only so many `StringName` objects you’re creating in a game (go ahead and count in your projects), and 2. The backing native `string_name` is also never removed from its cache. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2863254581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2863302291","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2863302291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2863302291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qqoaT","user":{"login":"lrahmann","id":9094802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9094802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann","html_url":"https://github.com/lrahmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T14:39:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T14:39:38Z","body":"@myblindy \r\nthis loop will leak if name is e.g. dynamic:\r\n`for(int i=0;i<1000;i++) StringName tmp = $\"{Name}/Node/In/Tree/{i}\";`\r\n\r\nLeak in the sense that this memory can not be freed again ever by the user because he can't access these StringName objects. \r\nNormally the finalizer would fix this, but the dictionary creates an additional reference. \r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2863302291/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2864964674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2864964674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2864964674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qw-RC","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T03:15:14Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T03:15:14Z","body":"I will reiterate that even if you wanted to protect against insane code like that (and I don’t), that is ~15kb of memory used. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2864964674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865056131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2865056131","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2865056131,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qxUmD","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T04:22:21Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T04:22:21Z","body":"In most cases there is no problem not releasing the cache. But Godot needs to consider all use cases. For example, caching the StringName of long texts in translation API may waste many RAM.\r\n \r\nIn GDScript, the script can automatically cache the conversion of constant strings to StringName. But in C# we can only either use weak references as cache, or expose the cache dict for users to clear it manually.\r\n \r\nThe problem is whether GodotSharp should have a built-in cache, or use Roslyn analyzer to let users deal with it manually #106096.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865056131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865350117","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2865350117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2865350117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qycXl","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T06:51:50Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T06:51:50Z","body":"Maybe we can only cache the string that [String.IsInterned](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.isinterned?view=net-9.0#system-string-isinterned(system-string)). Since interned strings are never released, it's reasonable to also keep the StringNames for them.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2865350117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869129618","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2869129618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2869129618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rA3GS","user":{"login":"fLindahl","id":18470258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDcwMjU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18470258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl","html_url":"https://github.com/fLindahl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T19:48:23Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T19:48:23Z","body":"My two cents is that it's better to let 99.9% of users avoid getting stutters that are hard to track and debug, than having 0.1% users run out of memory (which is easy to debug) because they construct 1 gazillion StringNames. So I think a built-in cache has benefits that outweigh the drawbacks.\r\n\r\nI do see that there might be high memory usage if there's a lot of long texts in translation apis. Could it be possible to add a configuration that turns the cache on/off, for the few cases where this might be an issue?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869129618/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869159589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2869159589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2869159589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rA-al","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T21:21:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T21:21:07Z","body":"> I do see that there might be high memory usage if there's a lot of long texts in translation apis. \r\n\r\nI have a feeling that the people who are getting stuck on this \"translation api\" thing might not understand what this PR does. It caches `StringName` instances created **only implicitly** from `string` objects. Explicit constructor calls, static cache instances, internal lookups due to translations, none of those are affected, only actual code that uses implicit `string` instances are changed -- for example, input lookups every frame.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869159589/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869498138","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2869498138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2869498138,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rCREa","user":{"login":"fLindahl","id":18470258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDcwMjU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18470258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl","html_url":"https://github.com/fLindahl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T05:40:06Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T05:42:19Z","body":"Alright good point, then it shouldn't be a problem.\n\nRealized that I was being somewhat ambiguous and I want to clarify my two cents: I support the PR because it's easier to debug memory leaks than stutters that happen sporadically.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869498138/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2883755513","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2883755513","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2883755513,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6r4p35","user":{"login":"lrahmann","id":9094802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9094802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann","html_url":"https://github.com/lrahmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-15T13:08:25Z","updated_at":"2025-05-15T13:08:25Z","body":"If you are set to use Dictionary clearly .IsInterned is the better approach, you could even log a warning when using the Auto Cast on a dynamic string. Otherwise I don't really see the issue with ConditionalWeakTable. \r\n\r\nGodot is very well written/strict in  terms of its memory tracking capabilities, so much that it can give you a list of un-freed StringNames  on exit. I would a bit surprised if this gets merged in this state.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2883755513/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887498367","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2887498367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2887498367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sG7p_","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T19:15:36Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T19:15:36Z","body":"> clearly .IsInterned is the better approach\r\n\r\nWhy is a boolean clearly the better approach? Are you confusing it with [`string.Intern`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.intern?view=net-9.0)? And if so, why is the performance hit of transforming every string clearly the better approach to fix frame stutters?\r\n\r\n> Godot is very well written/strict in terms of its memory tracking capabilities\r\n\r\nThat is exactly why a non-weak reference is better, so there is never overhead to allocate a new `StringName` when a black box system (Godot's native side, or the .Net GC) decides to free it. \r\n\r\nI will reiterate that I'd be a lot more impressed by these what-if scenarios if you could come up with actual hard numbers of bytes that would be kept in memory, to show how much is actually wasted in a real project. Even incredibly bad code like the above https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2863302291 is about 15k bytes.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887498367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892308708","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2892308708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2892308708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sZSDk","user":{"login":"lrahmann","id":9094802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9094802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann","html_url":"https://github.com/lrahmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T21:32:47Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T21:33:15Z","body":"> > clearly .IsInterned is the better approach\r\n> \r\n> Why is a boolean clearly the better approach? Are you confusing it with [`string.Intern`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.intern?view=net-9.0)? And if so, why is the performance hit of transforming every string clearly the better approach to fix frame stutters?\r\n> \r\n\r\nIf ``String.IsInterned(s) != null`` use the global static dict, otherwise don't (and maybe emit a warning somewhere). \r\nAll global Strings are interned by default, if a dynamic string matches a global string, IsInterned will return the global string. \r\n\r\n> > Godot is very well written/strict in terms of its memory tracking capabilities\r\n> \r\n> That is exactly why a non-weak reference is better, so there is never overhead to allocate a new `StringName` when a black box system (Godot's native side, or the .Net GC) decides to free it.\r\n> \r\n> I will reiterate that I'd be a lot more impressed by these what-if scenarios if you could come up with actual hard numbers of bytes that would be kept in memory, to show how much is actually wasted in a real project. Even incredibly bad code like the above [#106153 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2863302291) is about 15k bytes.\r\n\r\nGodot cannot free it until the finalizer has run, that is exactly what the finalizer is supposed to do.\r\n\r\nThe C# finalizer also has defined semantics. By using a [ConditionalWeakTable<String,StringName>](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.runtime.compilerservices.conditionalweaktable-2)\r\nthe finalizer of StringName will not run, as long as either of these two holds true:\r\n - there is a reference to the string used as the key \r\n - there is a reference to the StringName used as the value\r\n\r\nOnly if none of these conditions are met the StringName will eventually be freed.  If that happens one can assume that this string will not be needed any more. \r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892308708/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2913656742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2913656742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2913656742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tqt-m","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T19:07:19Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T19:07:19Z","body":"> If String.IsInterned(s) != null use the global static dict, otherwise don't (and maybe emit a warning somewhere).\r\nAll global Strings are interned by default, if a dynamic string matches a global string, IsInterned will return the global string.\r\n\r\nI know what interned strings are. The point is that this doesn't make any sense in this context. The only place the .Net string is used in is to look up in the dictionary (in case of a cache hit), and the string has to be constructed to do that in the first place. There is no benefit to doing something like `dict[string.Intern(s)]` vs `dict[s]`. \r\n\r\n> Godot cannot free it until the finalizer has run\r\n\r\nYes, and that's precisely what I want. \r\n\r\n> [long ChatGPT explanation of what Weak means]\r\n\r\nUnderstood, I don't want these objects to ever be freed just to be reallocated later. That is precisely the issue we're trying to fix. \r\n\r\n>  If that happens one can assume that this string will not be needed any more.\r\n\r\nThat is not a valid assumption. Just think of the most common pattern of using these `StringName` instances:\r\n\r\n```\r\npublic void _Process()\r\n{\r\n    if(Input.IsActionPressed(\"ui_accept\")) \r\n        // do stuff\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere there is no more reference to the `StringName` after the call, so the GC is free to recover it, thus invalidating your weak dictionary. Then the next frame it has to be reallocated from scratch, then it can get freed -- it's literally the pattern we're trying to fix.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2913656742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916438948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2916438948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2916438948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t1VOk","user":{"login":"lrahmann","id":9094802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9094802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann","html_url":"https://github.com/lrahmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lrahmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T13:50:28Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T13:50:28Z","body":"\r\n> ```\r\n> public void _Process()\r\n> {\r\n>     if(Input.IsActionPressed(\"ui_accept\")) \r\n>         // do stuff\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Here there is no more reference to the `StringName` after the call, so the GC is free to recover it, thus invalidating your weak dictionary. Then the next frame it has to be reallocated from scratch, then it can get freed -- it's literally the pattern we're trying to fix.\r\n\r\nHmm afaik this is not the case. The CLR normally doesn't free interned strings. While the docs are not super explicit about this see:\r\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.reflection.emit.opcodes.ldstr?view=net-9.0\r\n``The Common Language Infrastructure (CLI) guarantees that the result of two ldstr instructions referring to two metadata tokens that have the same sequence of characters return precisely the same string object (a process known as \"string interning\").``\r\nand \r\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/fundamentals/runtime-libraries/system-string-intern\r\n``First, the memory allocated for interned [String](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string) objects is not likely to be released until the common language runtime (CLR) terminates``\r\n\r\nHere is a JSFiddle using your example, notice how all the dynamic strings are actually removed by the GC:\r\nhttps://dotnetfiddle.net/sGerMp\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916438948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2968742520","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-2968742520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":2968742520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6w82p4","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T01:54:46Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T01:54:46Z","body":"This has nothing to do with interned strings, or any other kind of string. It's the `StringName` instance that's getting GC'd and we're trying to avoid. \r\n\r\nThough I should point out that interned strings also never get freed by the runtime (as per your own quote above) and .Net has survived just fine for over 20 years. Holding references to a few `StringName`s won't break Godot either. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2968742520/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3557927481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153#issuecomment-3557927481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106153","id":3557927481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UEao5","user":{"login":"Theome","id":668256,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2ODI1Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/668256?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome","html_url":"https://github.com/Theome","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Theome/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T12:58:20Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T12:58:20Z","body":"Is there a chance this will be reviewed/merged soon? \r\n\r\nI noticed that implicit `StringName` allocations are causing some trouble in my project. It looks like this PR 